# Leave unset so this window starts its own API (the packaged default).
# That process uses PGlite under userData. Set this only to attach to an
# already running Berry. Absolute http(s), no credentials. Use localhost —
# Next.js treats 127.0.0.1 as another origin and blocks /_next.
# BERRY_DESKTOP_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Optional host Postgres for the stack this window starts. A pglite:
# checkout DATABASE_URL is ignored so the window keeps its own data dir.
# BERRY_DESKTOP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/berry?sslmode=disable
# Aurora / RDS IAM: also copy DATABASE_IAM_AUTH and AWS_REGION (or AWS_PROFILE)
# from the checkout `.env` so the window's server can mint tokens.
